# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Odysseus — Gemini Web-Scraper LLM backend configuration
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Copy the lines you need into your main .env file (or export them in your
# shell), then start Odysseus normally:
#
#   uvicorn app:app --reload
#
# ── REQUIRED ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Set this to 1 to replace every LLM call with the Gemini web-scraper.
# No Ollama, no llama.cpp, no API keys needed.
ODYSSEUS_LLM_SCRAPER=1

# ── OPTIONAL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Run Chrome in headless mode (no visible window).
# Only useful after you have already logged into Google once with a
# persistent profile and SCRAPER_HEADLESS=0 (the default).
# SCRAPER_HEADLESS=0

# Override where the persistent Chrome profile is stored.
# Default: ~/.odysseus_chrome_profile
# SCRAPER_CHROME_PROFILE=/path/to/your/chrome/profile

# ── HOW IT WORKS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. On the first run Odysseus opens a visible Chrome window and navigates to
#    https://gemini.google.com/app.  Log into your Google account when prompted.
#
# 2. The session is saved in ~/.odysseus_chrome_profile.  All subsequent
#    starts reuse the saved login — no repeated sign-in.
#
# 3. Every chat message is serialised into a single history-replay prompt,
#    injected into the Gemini text box via JavaScript, submitted, and the
#    response is extracted once it stops changing (stable-for-4.5 s heuristic).
#
# 4. The full response is then chunked into ~80-character SSE delta frames
#    so the Odysseus chat UI receives it as a streaming reply.
#
# ── LIMITATIONS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# • Gemini's web UI cannot perform native function/tool-calls, so the agent
#   loop's tool-use features degrade to plain conversational replies.
# • Each request resets the Gemini chat to prevent context bleed, which adds
#   a ~3-5 s navigation overhead per message.
# • Automating a web UI is inherently fragile; a Gemini DOM update can break
#   the CSS selectors used by the scraper.  If responses stop appearing, check
#   the selectors in src/scraper_llm.py (_wait_and_extract_response).
# • Using the Gemini web UI programmatically may violate Google's Terms of Service.
#   Use at your own discretion.
